{com}. 
. * ==============================================================================
. * 3. Estimate spillovers for WOS publication outcomes
. * ==============================================================================
. 
. use ${c -(}RUN5_STATA_WOS{c )-}CN_WOS_DID.dta, clear
{txt}
{com}. 
. drop if wos_field==""
{txt}(169 observations deleted)

{com}. 
. * Construct WOS publication-based firm-size categories.
. bys firm_id: egen size = sum (pub_num)
{txt}
{com}. 
. gen size_category = 0
{txt}
{com}. replace size_category=1 if size==0 //0-25%
{txt}(0 real changes made)

{com}. replace size_category=2 if size==1 //25%-50%
{txt}(692,094 real changes made)

{com}. replace size_category=3 if size==2 //50%-75%
{txt}(183,131 real changes made)

{com}. replace size_category=4 if size>=3 //75%-100%
{txt}(277,862 real changes made)

{com}. 
. 
. bys wos_field size_category year: egen did_spillover = max(did) // considering spillover effect
{txt}
{com}. drop if entity_list==1 // drop original treatment group
{txt}(9,815 observations deleted)

{com}. 
. * Estimate the level outcome using linear fixed effects.
. reghdfe pub_num_w did_spillover, absorb(firm_id year) vce(r)
{res}{txt}({browse "http://scorreia.com/research/hdfe.pdf":MWFE estimator} converged in 2 iterations)
